## What changed per finding

1. Census derived from the Go types (`members_test.go`
   rewritten): a reflection walk over both input types (nested
   structs, slices of structs, maps; unhandled kinds fail loudly)
   yields every shape member with its JSON type and nullability via
   a mechanical snake_case rule plus 4 documented irregular names
   (`expected_target_native_session_id`, `target_resource_keys`,
   `expected_disposition`, `insertion_after_event_id`); synthesized
   top-level members derive by sealed set difference; the exact-set
   test cross-checks derived vs sealed in both directions.
   Miscased sweep covers 6 variant classes (upper, lower,
   title-first, title-segments, toggle-first, toggle-last);
   duplication surgery covers EVERY member via a byte-path splicer.
   `TestMemberCensusNoLiteralList` guards the derivation (AST scan
   trips at 10+ member names, 40%+ purity; a planted 12-name list
   reddened it and removal greened it). The reviewer's Titlecase
   plant is killed by `TestMemberCensusMiscased` ALONE (adopted as
   harness row `N-case-title-strategy`, byte-identical edit).
2. DAG whole domain (`dag_test.go` rewritten):
   `TestDAGWholeDomainCensus` classifies EVERY graph through 4
   operations (2+16+512+65536) against the oracle through both
   entries, and at 5 operations drives every edge class
   (self/equal, higher, lower, missing, unsorted, duplicate) at
   every position. `TestDAGValidEnumerationFive` admits all 1024
   valid 5-DAGs; `TestDAGSingleEdgeLocality` (35 toggles) and
   `TestDAGLocalityStructure` (AST pin: 3 range loops, calls subset
   of make/len/invalid, `>=` lower rule, single presence store,
   negated lookup) prove the per-edge-local rule. The reviewer's
   4-op self-edge plant is killed by the census ALONE (adopted as
   `N-dagfour-self`, byte-identical edit).
3. Entry grid (`nullability_test.go` rewritten):
   `TestEntryNullabilityGrid` sweeps kind x all 2^3 presence
   combinations x mode (48 cells) through BOTH manifest entries
   against the oracle; every refuse cell asserts a structural
   literal (branch phrases on build, unknown/missing member codes
   on decode, which fire before the self-digest check).
   `TestEntryGridNeverPanics` sweeps the same grid under per-cell
   recovery. The reviewer's branchcombo plant is killed by the
   grid ALONE via the panic guard (adopted as
   `N-entry-branch-combo`, byte-identical edit). Production keeps
   no redundant nil checks: they would mask the shipped
   single-member branch narrowings.
4. Hygiene: the harness EOF blank line is removed; the scratch-
   index `git diff --cached --check` over the full candidate
   (tracked + untracked, real index untouched) exits 0.
5. Notes closed: `TestMappingCountMillionEntryLevel` seals and
   decodes exactly 1,000,000 mappings and refuses 1,000,001 with
   the count literal on BOTH entries (31s; skips under
   `-short` like the 65536 precedent); `N-count-mapping-max` now
   kills at the entry test. The importer grid is keyed
   (package, entry, input): 22 reused owner entries x input
   classes, base vs candidate, with 171 files hash-compared
   identical and owner suites green on both trees — no moved
   class. The build zero census extends to nested plan members
   with reflection-count guards on every table.

